  "correction_rules": [
    "When sentiment history shows a sustained positive trend (e.g., >0.33), model tends to overestimate prices; reduce forecast by 5-10% in such periods.",
    "After a sharp price spike (e.g., >10% from prior day), model often overshoots; apply a 1-2 day lag correction to avoid overreaction.",
    "In low-sentiment periods (sentiment ≤ 0.00), model underestimates prices; adjust upward by 3-5% to capture mean reversion.",
    "When history shows a clear downward trend (e.g., 3 consecutive days < 65), model fails to recognize mean reversion; increase forecast by 2-5% to align with trend reversal.",
    "For long-term forecasts (30-day horizon), model tends to underestimate price volatility; add 1-2% volatility buffer to forecast range."
  ]
}
